DOCUMENT();

#############
# Load Macros
#############

loadMacros(
  "PGstandard.pl",
  "PGML.pl",
  "AnswerFormatHelp.pl",
  "PCCmacros.pl",
  "parserNumberWithUnits.pl",
  "parserLinearRelation.pl",
  "ORCCA.pl",
  "PGcourse.pl",
);
COMMENT('Authored in PreTeXt');

#######
# Setup
#######

$initial = 100;
$start = NumberWithUnits("$initial lb");
$rate = random(7,12);
$speed = NumberWithUnits("$rate lb");
$final = random(20,30,5);
$end = NumberWithUnits("$final lb");
Context("LinearRelation")->variables->are(t => 'Real');
$equation = LinearRelation("$initial - $rate t = $final");

#############################
# Exercise Group Introduction
#############################

BEGIN_PGML
Write an equation to model the scenario. There is no need to solve the equation.

END_PGML

######
# Body
######

BEGIN_PGML
A restaurant stocks its pantry with [`[$start]`] of onions. When the supply reaches [`[$end]\text{,}`] it's time to order more. Recently, the restaurant has been using [`[$speed]`] of onions per day. How long since restocking will it take until another order must be placed? Write an equation to model this scenario. There is no need to solve it.

[@KeyboardInstructions('Use [|t|]* as the variable.')@]**

[_]{$equation}{20}

END_PGML

#############
# End Problem
#############

ENDDOCUMENT();
